course: dictionary
lesson: 16033
title: Checkable words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell us whether something can be proved. Verifiable is one of them: it means able to be checked and shown to be true or false. «The recipe says the cake bakes in 30 minutes.» You can check that by baking the cake and watching the clock.
explain: Compare that with an opinion: «The cake tastes the best in the world.» This cannot be checked in the same way, because everyone has different tastes. Opinions are not verifiable. Ask yourself: could someone test this and get a clear answer?
explain: A verifiable source is a book, website or person whose facts can be checked. «The science book gives the height of the mountain, and a map from the survey office gives the same height.» Good writers use sources you can check, not rumours.
fact: Verifiable means able to be checked and shown to be true or false.
fact: Verifiable facts are facts you can test or look up to prove them.
fact: A rumour is a story that spreads without proof, so it is not verifiable until someone checks it.
fact: An opinion says what someone thinks or feels, such as «Dogs are the best pets», and it cannot be proved true or false.
fact: Verifiable comes from verify, meaning to check, plus -able, meaning able to be.
exercise: «The sun rose at 6:14 this morning, and the weather office recorded the time.» Is this verifiable? | *Yes, it can be checked against the records | No, it is a story with no facts in it | No, it is only someone's opinion
exercise: Which of these is a verifiable fact? | Everyone should love the colour blue | Football is the most boring sport | *Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius at sea level
exercise: Which word means able to be checked and shown true or false? | *Verifiable | Loud | Beautiful | Sleepy
test: Mum says the library is open until 5 o'clock, and the sign on the door says so. Is the opening time verifiable? | *Yes, you can check the sign or phone the library | No, it is just her favourite idea | No, only a guess can ever be checked
test: Which sentence is an opinion, not a verifiable fact? | Ice is frozen water | Light travels faster than sound | *The painting is the most beautiful in the world
exam: Which is the best source for a verifiable fact about a volcano's height? | *A science book or official survey that gives the measured height | A rumour a friend heard at school | A dream you had about the volcano | A guess written on the back of a crisp packet
